  'oraub2m9': `
`%s %s= %s` is not supported: an index read returns an option (nil when out of range), so a compound assignment would evaluate the index twice and discard the failure. Rewrite it as (the `it` of the ok arm is the element slot, readable and writable):
     %s: {
         ok -> it = it %s %s
         -> _
     }
   or `%s ?= %s %s %s` (propagates the failure; requires the enclosing function to have an option result parameter)
`
